WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.746
Hey guys, as you may know, i did a tedx talk in the summer about my experience with

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:09.471
the lion diet, the all meat diet that put my autoimmune disorder that caused crippling

00:00:09.521 --> 00:00:15.325
arthritis and gave me two joint replacements into remission. I followed Tedx's guidelines

00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:20.774
very carefully, as i'm aware my experience with diet is anecdotal. I finished the

00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:26.061
talk asking the medical system to look into the diet further. We spent the last four

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:31.207
months going back and forth with tedx because they won't post the talk. I was the

00:00:31.257 --> 00:00:36.365
only talk from that tedx conference that they refused to post. They said my talk

00:00:36.415 --> 00:00:41.015
went against their community guidelines, but couldn't name exactly what it went against,

00:00:41.065 --> 00:00:47.213
and it didn't. Like i said, i was really careful. Since then, harvard has put out

00:00:47.263 --> 00:00:51.510
a study on the carnivore diet that i've linked below showing other people who have

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.643
also had success putting their diseases into remission. This is something that should

00:00:56.693 --> 00:01:01.672
be taken seriously and looked into. Tedx is supposed to be a place for new ideas

00:01:01.722 --> 00:01:06.958
and novel thinking and anecdotal reports. They have tons of vegan talks claiming

00:01:07.008 --> 00:01:12.197
veganism cures diseases. But my story didn't make it through because it violated

00:01:12.247 --> 00:01:18.166
community guidelines they can't name so i decided to put it up here. Enjoy. Hi, my

00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:23.311
name is Mikhaila Peterson and i'm here to talk about how i put my idiopathic autoimmune

00:01:23.361 --> 00:01:28.077
disorder and mood disorder and chronic fatigue into remission with an extreme elimination

00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:34.340
diet of only eating meat. But i will start at the beginning. When i was two, i started

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:39.309
walking with my feet out like a duck and by the time i was in grade 2, i was walking

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.654
down stairs one foot at a time complaining that my shoes were too small and i was

00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:48.200
diagnosed with juvenile rheumatoid arthritis active in 37 joints.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:54.598
I was put on methotrexate and naproxen to get my symptoms under control and had cortisone

00:01:54.648 --> 00:02:00.973
injected into 17 of my joints. In grade 2 i was sitting on a chair in class because

00:02:01.023 --> 00:02:05.330
i couldn't sit on the carpet because i couldn't sit on my knees or cross my legs.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.876
I was using this really ugly fat pencil because i couldn't hold a pencil because i couldn't close my hand.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:19.537
When i was in grade 4, i was put on enbrel, a biologic immune suppressant and i started

00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:24.878
injecting myself with enbrel and methotrexate twice a week and i was put into a medically

00:02:24.928 --> 00:02:30.538
induced remission and i went on all the sports teams i could go on. I went from being

00:02:30.588 --> 00:02:35.863
nearly wheelchair bound to playing sports. At the same time my mental health declined

00:02:35.913 --> 00:02:41.094
dramatically and i started experiencing OCD symptoms and suicidal thoughts and i

00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:46.912
was put on SSRIs and diagnosed with major depressive disorder potentially bipolar type 2 with hypomania.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.056
When i was in grade 8, i started experiencing the sensations of mosquitoes biting my whole body.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.758
And chronic fatigue. And by chronic fatigue, I mean I couldn't wake up and i was falling asleep in class.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:08.390
By the time i was in grade 11, my arthritis had gotten bad enough that it had destroyed

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.962
all the cartilage in my right hip and i stopped being able to sleep because of the

00:03:13.012 --> 00:03:19.200
pain and was put on oxycontin. And when i was 17, i had my hip replaced.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:27.122
While i was healing from my hip replacement, my body destroyed all the cartilage in

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:32.400
my left ankle and i ended up walking on basically broken bones.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.600
So i had my ankle replaced, so that was 17.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:43.035
I went off to university and my mental health deteriorated further. They tried to

00:03:43.085 --> 00:03:48.546
stabilize me with wellbutrin and i ended up having a grand mal seizure at the university

00:03:48.596 --> 00:03:54.938
library. They tried to stabilize me with an SNRI and i was so angry i felt like i

00:03:54.988 --> 00:04:00.610
could claw my skin off. But a year and a half into university (this gets better, i swear) about a year and a half...

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:09.368
About a year and a half into university, I was so fatigued that i missed my final exams and i dropped out and went home.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.927
When i got home, i started experiencing a rash on my back and on my bum and then on

00:04:17.977 --> 00:04:22.200
my face and when i got to my face i thought, okay arthritis is one thing,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.869
Idiopathic hypersomnia or chronic fatigue is one thing,&nbsp;Chronic depression is one

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:33.489
thing,&nbsp;but like a rash on my face? I cannot handle that and i started researching.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.000
December 2014, the rash stopped healing!

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.038
And i went to dermatologist after dermatologist and they said, you know, stop doing

00:04:43.088 --> 00:04:47.700
this. You're anxious. I was like, okay, that's not super helpful.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.433
So i figured if i don't figure out what's wrong with me, i'm going to die because

00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:58.664
my body was destroying its tissues. At that point i was on tylenol 3 to take at night

00:04:58.714 --> 00:05:02.672
because the shoulder pain was so bad from the arthritis that wasn't kept in check

00:05:02.722 --> 00:05:07.614
that i couldn't sleep. I was taking 40 milligrams of adderall just to wake up in

00:05:07.664 --> 00:05:12.100
the morning, because of the ideopathic hypersomnia, i was taking dapsone, which is

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:17.298
used in antibiotic use to treat leprosy so that my skin would heal. I was taking

00:05:17.348 --> 00:05:22.265
40 milligrams of Escitalopram for the depression. I was taking an inhaler because

00:05:22.315 --> 00:05:27.136
if i got a cold, it would turn into bronchitis that would turn into pneumonia. And

00:05:27.186 --> 00:05:32.589
I'd end up in the hospital because of the immune suppressants. I was taking a prescription-strength

00:05:32.639 --> 00:05:37.254
antihistamine because i was so allergic to trees and grass that i was verging on

00:05:37.304 --> 00:05:42.472
anaphylaxis in the spring. Anyway there were more. So i started researching and i

00:05:42.522 --> 00:05:47.059
came across this rash eventually called dermatitis herpetiformis, which is the skin

00:05:47.109 --> 00:05:51.577
manifestation of celiac disease, which is an autoimmune disorder that can be triggered

00:05:51.627 --> 00:05:57.467
by gluten. And i thought, holy shit is it celiac disease the whole time? so i cut

00:05:57.517 --> 00:06:02.225
out gluten. I went off of my immune suppressants, which weren't really working anyway

00:06:02.275 --> 00:06:06.553
given the fact i'd lost a hip and ankle and i started monitoring my symptoms really

00:06:06.603 --> 00:06:12.616
closely to look for flare-ups. In september 2015 i reduced my diet further because

00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:16.571
cutting out gluten wasn't enough and i thought if i'm going to be doing this for

00:06:16.621 --> 00:06:21.077
the rest of my life, researching, trying to figure out what's wrong with me, i might

00:06:21.127 --> 00:06:26.264
as well rule out diet. So i went down to meat and greens and certain root vegetables

00:06:26.314 --> 00:06:31.488
that i didn't really like, like carrots, sweet potatoes, parsnips. I cut out all

00:06:31.538 --> 00:06:36.144
the foods that i thought could be potentially causing inflammation. And that month,

00:06:36.194 --> 00:06:41.270
my skin healed for the first time in a number of years. I lost three pant sizes of bloating I didn't know i had.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.661
Two months into that, my fatigue went away for the first time since grade 8 and i

00:06:49.711 --> 00:06:56.014
stopped taking adderall. Three months into that diet, my depression went away for

00:06:56.064 --> 00:07:01.182
the first time in my entire life and i went from living in hell to being in heaven

00:07:01.232 --> 00:07:04.000
a hell that i didn't know i'd been living in.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:11.206
And i thought, okay, well, i'm not taking any drugs ever again and i stopped taking

00:07:11.256 --> 00:07:17.253
my SSRI over a two-week period without realizing - because nobody told me - that

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:24.722
SSRI withdrawal exists. And for the next two years, i had the most horrifying experiences

00:07:24.772 --> 00:07:27.600
of my entire life and that is saying something.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:34.386
I reintroduced soy a couple of weeks after i went off of SSRIs and i had a full-blown autoimmune response.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:42.749
And it started with my digestion was upset. My entire body got itchy. The next day

00:07:42.799 --> 00:07:47.434
my depression was back worse than i'd ever experienced. I got into the shower and

00:07:47.484 --> 00:07:51.363
thought, how could i be so arrogant as to think i could control this disease with

00:07:51.413 --> 00:07:57.386
diet? and i cried. Four days later i had mouth ulcers. My arthritis was back, my

00:07:57.436 --> 00:08:01.000
rash was back and i got my brother to drive me home from my parents

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:08.300
because i didn't think i could drive. And i got out of the car and i went to my apartment.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:13.977
I turned around and my brothers head looked like that for about 2 seconds he looked

00:08:14.027 --> 00:08:18.671
at me and he went off and then it was my brother again and i thought, oh my god i

00:08:18.721 --> 00:08:22.300
just stop taking all my medications and now i'm insane.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.070
So for the next year i went in and out of what i now know was SSRI withdrawal mixed

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:34.225
with an autoimmune disorder and food sensitivities. And i had 24-day-long reactions

00:08:34.275 --> 00:08:36.200
each time i tried to reintroduce a food.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.723
About a year after that, i figured maybe i'll just stop reintroducing foods and not

00:08:40.773 --> 00:08:44.547
experience this. And at that time, i got pregnant, which i didn't even know i would

00:08:44.597 --> 00:08:46.800
be able to do, given all the medications i've been on.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.131
I went down to meat and greens to try and get my symptoms under control and a year

00:08:52.181 --> 00:08:56.825
after that that i was breastfeeding, getting out of bed. My wrist buckled. I thought,

00:08:56.875 --> 00:09:02.021
okay i have to do something because i'm worried i'm going to drop my baby. The arthritis

00:09:02.071 --> 00:09:07.091
was back, i was itchy everywhere and i was like, how is this possible? if i'd experienced

00:09:07.141 --> 00:09:11.494
remission, why isn't that diet working anymore? and i cut everything out except for beef.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:19.213
And two weeks after doing that, thinking i'm nuts and hopefully i don't get vitamin deficiencies,

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.000
the itch went away and my joints started to feel better.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:29.694
Four weeks after that, so six weeks after an all-beef diet, the depression lifted

00:09:29.744 --> 00:09:33.470
and i stopped crying in the morning and five months after that, the anxiety lifted

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:38.059
and i was back in what i felt was heaven compared to how i'd been living. So that's

00:09:38.109 --> 00:09:43.296
all beef, all lamb, salt, and water. Now i've been talking about this diet, to spread

00:09:43.346 --> 00:09:46.987
awareness in hopes that the medical community can take something like this seriously.

00:09:47.037 --> 00:09:52.295
My mom went on the diet and her osteoarthritis went away. My dad went on the diet

00:09:52.345 --> 00:09:57.978
and he lost 70 pounds. His GERDs went away, he had psoriasis that went away. I've

00:09:58.028 --> 00:10:02.123
talked to thousands of people with autoimmune disorders who have done similar things and seen similar results.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:11.656
So that is me now and that is my kid. I'm a CEO, i'm a podcaster. I try to share my

00:10:11.706 --> 00:10:16.998
experience to get people to see what this kind of diet does for me. I called it The

00:10:17.048 --> 00:10:21.505
Lion Diet because it's not cool to be this restricted and it's not cool to have an

00:10:21.555 --> 00:10:27.759
autoimmune disorder. And people who are sick feel isolated and miserable. So i'm

00:10:27.809 --> 00:10:33.287
trying to make it cool. But what would be really cool would be if the medical community

00:10:33.337 --> 00:10:36.200
could take this seriously and do some case studies.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.200
That's it.

